1
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:34,000
I kick a pebble and my shoes go flying too,

3
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:42,260
right onto the head of the
carpenter who'd been saving up.

4
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:48,440
They laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:55,220
Even if you lose your spirit,
Katsushika Kameari.

6
00:00:55,220 --> 00:01:02,540
Even the yawns are the same,
but the streetscape is strangely gentle.

7
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:10,440
From the water intake
tower with its pointed cap,

8
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:16,780
the sun sinks into the
great canopy of the sky.

9
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow too,
it'll end just like this, won't it.

10
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,280
Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost again.

11
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:33,860
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

12
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,780
Good morning.

13
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:54,820
What are you doing, Chief?

14
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:56,100
Morning.

15
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:00,840
Well, a video letter arrived from my daughter,
with footage of my grandson Daisuke.

16
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:04,180
So I bought a camcorder to send a reply.

17
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,740
Ever since, I've been completely hooked.

18
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:09,420
The Chief is into video recording now?

19
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:14,260
These days anyone can enjoy a camcorder casually,
it's the AV era after all.

20
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,463
Come to think of it,

21
00:02:15,513 --> 00:02:18,940
I often see people filming
kids at parks and such.

22
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:23,620
Yet I barely have any photos
left from my own childhood.

23
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:25,360
Ryotsu, you want to watch too?

24
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:28,580
The videos I shot of Daisuke are adorable.

25
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:30,000
No, thank you.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,640
Those things are only fun for the family.

27
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:41,060
It's just boring. When I visit people's homes, some parents keep showing
their kids' videos endlessly. It's nothing but torture.

28
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:45,500
Besides,
I can already imagine the Chief's videos.

29
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:52,800
Amateur footage full of pointless long takes, shaky hands, out-of-focus shots,
and failed zooms. If you film while walking, you'd probably trip.

30
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:58,180
So you'd end up filming nothing but your own feet. Just thinking about it,
I'm sure the picture would be terrible.

31
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:03,180
Idiot! You're an amateur, so how could
you possibly film that well from the start!

32
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:08,580
Even a clumsy video is a fine work if
it overflows with love for the child!

33
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,320
That's enough. I won't show you anything.

34
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:14,520
Sorry, we were so looking
forward to your masterpiece.

35
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,580
Well then, I'll go out on patrol.

36
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:19,780
How cruel, Ryo-chan.

37
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:20,960
Really.

38
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:24,120
Well? Do you want to see them?
The videos I shot.

39
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,640
W-well, of course.

40
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:27,260
I-I'd really love to see them!

41
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:30,360
That's right,
I have to go on patrol with my senior.

42
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:31,380
Kei-chan.

43
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:35,500
That's right,
patrols are always done in pairs.

44
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:36,700
Come on, Reiko.

45
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:37,480
Y-yes.

46
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,140
I'm off!

47
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:47,720
Cut!

48
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:51,000
No good, no good. The expression is stiff.

49
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:55,300
Listen, shutter, this is a video
library that will last a lifetime!

50
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:57,320
With a more natural smile.

51
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:58,860
One more time.

52
00:03:58,860 --> 00:03:59,460
Okay!

53
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:05,040
Alright, Scene 1, Cut 3, Take 5.

54
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:06,680
Ready, action!

55
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:08,180
I'm off!

56
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:09,320
Cut, cut, cut!

57
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:13,120
Be more childlike and express
your joy with your whole body.

58
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:13,720
Got it?

59
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,040
Today is the fun sports day!

60
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:18,720
It goes like this: lan-ran-lan-ran-lan!

61
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,820
Today is the fun sports day!

62
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:22,240
Lan-ran-lan-ran-lan!

63
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,520
Don't say it out loud.

64
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:25,340
Express it with your body.

65
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:27,560
Alright, let's go again.

66
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,200
Okay!

67
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:35,420
Next is the scene where you
eagerly run all the way to school.

68
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:38,940
Run lightly on your feet to that tape mark.

69
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:40,900
Are you ready?

70
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:43,580
On your marks, get set, go!

71
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:45,860
Let's do our best at today's sports day!

72
00:04:46,380 --> 00:04:47,820
We're definitely going for first place!

73
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:53,780
Hey, don't stop on your own!

74
00:04:53,780 --> 00:04:55,100
But the dog...

75
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:55,960
No buts!

76
00:04:55,960 --> 00:05:03,860
I told you over and over that ad-libbing lines that aren't in the script is forbidden!
What's the problem? It's just a dog. Just jump over it and keep going, don't worry about it!

77
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:05,020
Don't do it on your own.

78
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:28,220
Let go! Let go! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

79
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:29,240
That's a natural expression.

80
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,680
Let's go to the sports day!

81
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,460
The rails came loose!

82
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:36,000
It's a slope.

83
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:38,040
Daddy!

84
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:39,280
H-help!

85
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:40,560
What?

86
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:42,680
Help!

87
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,400
Nakagawa's here!

88
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:44,820
Yes.

89
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:57,820
Are you alright?

90
00:05:57,820 --> 00:05:59,340
I'm not alright.

91
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:01,600
The camera's gone!

92
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:10,700
Thank goodness, it's fine. That was close.

93
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:13,600
You care more about
the camera than yourself?

94
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:16,880
Please don't help people so roughly.

95
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:19,960
In that situation, we had to do that
or he wouldn't have stopped, right?

96
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,980
It's an expensive camera, you know.

97
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:23,620
How completely insensitive!

98
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,200
What did you say?

99
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:29,680
Dad, we're really going to
be late for the sports day!

100
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,720
Right, that's right, I remember now.

101
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:33,680
We shouldn't be doing this right now.

102
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:36,640
Let's shoot the rest of the scenes later.

103
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:38,680
I see, so it's a sports day.

104
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:41,220
Still, what heavy equipment you've got!

105
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:46,420
A child's sports day is the biggest event for parents with video cameras,
after all.

106
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:53,080
What's wrong?
Carrying such heavy-looking luggage?

107
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:55,980
I'm delivering something my husband forgot.

108
00:06:56,820 --> 00:07:00,180
It's got a video battery
and all sorts of things in it.

109
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:01,740
It's just so heavy.

110
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:06,640
Are you by any chance the man
with glasses and the big backpack?

111
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:09,340
Yes, there's a sports day today.

112
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:18,800
Let us carry it for you. It's hard for a woman with something this heavy.
Where's the school? We'll carry it. Thank you, officer.

113
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:32,380
A turtle, with a shell, and a camera-san... Well, what a perfect name for a cameraman!
That would be fine, but my husband's name is written with the characters for "city" and "person," and it's read as Pinto.

114
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:33,300
Pinto?

115
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:35,960
Well, the number one is read as
"pin," that's true.

116
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:37,720
Then what's your son's name?

117
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:41,780
Yes, the "sha" from shashin, and the
"ta" from Taro. Shutter.

118
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:45,700
Focus and shutter That's too perfect.

119
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:49,860
Don't tell me your wife's name is Zoom
or Aperture or something like that.

120
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:52,680
No, it's Developing-and-Printing-ko.

121
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,300
Hey.

122
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:57,120
I'm joking. My name's Asako.

123
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:58,680
That's way too silly!

124
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,920
Asako, ASA.

125
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:04,120
Isn't that about film sensitivity?

126
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:09,160
Wow, it's like this family was born
to be stuck in the world of cameras.

127
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,620
I said it's fine, didn't I?

128
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:14,780
What the hell is this?!

129
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:17,360
What an incredible number of scenes.

130
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:20,300
It's like an idol photo shoot.

131
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:22,980
Finding anyone in this
crowd is going to be tough.

132
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:27,800
Sure, sports day is a great chance to film video,
but this is just too much.

133
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:33,020
Some parents are even checking monitors and
editing while their kids aren't competing!

134
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:37,000
Would you like videotapes?
We also have batteries!

135
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:39,960
The vendors are certainly
doing brisk business.

136
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:44,400
Sports days have changed a lot from the old days
when everyone just relaxed and ate rice balls.

137
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:46,200
Over there...

138
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:51,530
Hey, you there,

139
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:56,960
you forgot something.

140
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:58,660
Sorry, sorry.

141
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:00,360
You two,

142
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:04,060
the lady looked like she was
struggling with that heavy load,

143
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:06,180
so we went to help carry it.

144
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:07,700
I see.

145
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:08,920
Well, thanks a lot.

146
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,900
Still, that's an amazing camera.

147
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:12,120
You can tell?

148
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:13,740
Just by looking at it.

149
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:17,940
Fitted with a super telephoto
lens on a professional camera,

150
00:09:17,940 --> 00:09:20,560
this is a specially
modified sports-day camera!

151
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,640
These cheap run-of-the-mill videos,

152
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:23,740
I'll blow them all away!

153
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:25,700
Now that's serious equipment.

154
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:28,220
The focus lives up to its name.

155
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:33,000
This is the ultimate Video-dō!

156
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:37,880
We now begin the
third-graders' obstacle race.

157
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:40,400
Time for the shutter to shine!

158
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:45,440
Officer, hurry and connect the cable
to this professional D2 video deck!

159
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:47,620
Let's go.

160
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:49,900
Charge!

161
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:52,440
Eight-millimeter is fine, eight-millimeter!

162
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,900
Cheap cameras, move aside,
move aside, move aside!

163
00:09:55,740 --> 00:09:58,480
At this distance, a 6x zoom is useless!

164
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:01,000
Make way! You're in the way!

165
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:04,200
Saving a spot is like a battlefield!

166
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:05,140
Ready... set!

167
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:19,820
Chance!

168
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:27,040
Great! Powerful footage!

169
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:30,800
W-wait! Running around like that?!

170
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:36,000
Why does this have to happen to me...

171
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:44,040
Now it's a complete standstill!

172
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:53,480
Huff... huff... huff... huff...

173
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,260
Aaaaaaaah!

174
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:05,460
Good, Shutter!

175
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:08,400
What?!

176
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,900
Now it's the muddy crossing!

177
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:12,960
Aaaaaaaah!

178
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,440
Aaaaaaaah...

179
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:23,240
A magnificent masterpiece!

180
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:25,980
Well, that's good to hear.

181
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,840
Thank you so much for everything.

182
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:33,840
Man, what a terrible ordeal.
I'm covered in scrapes all over.

183
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:36,280
Thanks to you, I got some good footage.

184
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,420
Please, drop by my place if you like.

185
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,360
Something cold to drink, perhaps?

186
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:43,600
Oh no, I nearly forgot the final scene!

187
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,580
We're filming the kids coming home from
sports day with the sunset behind them!

188
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:51,420
He's still filming? What an energetic man.

189
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:54,400
Officer, it's not that way.

190
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:56,960
What, don't you live
in that housing complex?

191
00:11:57,660 --> 00:12:00,520
That's our home over there;
the video stuff is this way.

192
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:02,880
Aren't you a TV broadcaster?

193
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,920
I've been at a loss for
where to put all these tapes.

194
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:07,780
I bought it secondhand,
partly for its practicality.

195
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:08,820
Well, please, come in.

196
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:14,980
That's an amazing number of videotapes!

197
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:18,340
Since Shutter was born,
I've been filming him nonstop.

198
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:22,800
Five hours every day, up to his current age of eight.
I've compiled 5,500 tapes.

199
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:25,160
That's not what I'd call
a compiled number, is it?

200
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:27,820
There are still 2,000 unedited tapes.

201
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:30,560
Video is Shutter's treasure.

202
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:34,940
When he grows up, he'll surely be grateful
that you recorded his growth this much.

203
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:38,800
the day will come when he
sincerely thanks you for your love.

204
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,040
How do you watch all of them?

205
00:12:41,220 --> 00:12:45,100
Even just this lot, watching one
a day would take over fifteen years.

206
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:49,040
That's exactly why we can be moved by the depth of parental love,
isn't it?

207
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:52,280
There are no other parents who go this far.

208
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:54,760
Well, please, have something cold to drink.

209
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:58,660
This is Shutter at six months old.

210
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:02,040
Did you see? So far,

211
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:05,520
this expression, this angle,
it's a masterpiece.

212
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:10,260
Next is his kindergarten entrance ceremony.

213
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:13,320
Just look at these falling cherry blossoms.

214
00:13:13,320 --> 00:13:16,000
So dreamlike, it evokes such poetry.

215
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,500
Truly a masterpiece.

216
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,560
This richly layered contrast.

217
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:21,880
A zoom that cuts in sharply.

218
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:23,440
A smooth, flowing pan.

219
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:24,160
Masterpiece.

220
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:24,940
Masterpiece.

221
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:26,240
It's a masterpiece.

222
00:13:28,660 --> 00:13:29,760
What do you say?

223
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:32,660
That must have been hard.

224
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:35,760
Getting all the way up
here is really something.

225
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:37,660
I can't put up with this anymore.

226
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:42,680
They should've just quietly
watched Chief Ohara's video.

227
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:43,420
Officers!

228
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:45,060
Officers!

229
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:45,960
It's a real emergency.

230
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:47,840
I think Shutter has run away from home.

231
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:48,980
What?

232
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:50,020
Shutter-kun?

233
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:54,700
Well, I suggested we go shoot the sports-day
close-ups we missed yesterday this afternoon,

234
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:56,680
and he suddenly ran off.

235
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:19,120
There he is!

236
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:19,960
Hey!

237
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:20,580
Hold on a second!

238
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:22,520
This would make a great picture!

239
00:14:22,580 --> 00:14:23,880
This isn't the time for that!

240
00:14:24,380 --> 00:14:25,500
Mm, nice!

241
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:28,820
This light, this angle, what a poetic image!

242
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:36,740
Wonderful! The reflection off the water
creates a beautiful silhouette effect!

243
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:39,080
Never mind your photography nerd stuff,
just get going already!

244
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:45,660
Shutter, it'll be dark soon. Let's go home!

245
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:47,480
Why?

246
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:51,060
Dad likes video more than he likes me.

247
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:52,660
That's not true.

248
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:55,780
Because you're always just filming videos,

249
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:59,240
you won't even talk to
me unless you're filming!

250
00:14:59,240 --> 00:15:00,080
Shutter!

251
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:02,280
How long are you going to keep filming!

252
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:05,400
Hey, this is the best part!

253
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:11,180
I don't want to go home! I hate you, Dad!

254
00:15:12,140 --> 00:15:16,060
Damn, I missed that expression.
One more time.

255
00:15:16,060 --> 00:15:17,760
Nice!

256
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:21,180
Can't you understand how this boy feels?

257
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:24,440
W-what a convincing performance!

258
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:29,040
Then that's it. I'll take this boy in.

259
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:35,100
The way they walk away is wonderful too.

260
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:38,240
Alright, okay, this is a masterpiece!

261
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:47,260
Here you go, thanks.
So you ended up looking after Shutter?

262
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:57,220
If that old man has no child to film, he'll surely reconsider.
Dad's always like that. Even when I fall or drown, he's watching me through the camera.

263
00:15:57,780 --> 00:16:05,280
He cares more about the video than his wife, you know. That's not true.
There's no parent who doesn't think their child is important.

264
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:08,140
I film Chatta-kun because he's adorable.

265
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,520
But that went too far.

266
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:16,540
What's wrong, senpai?

267
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:19,980
No, something just flashed
in the park across the way.

268
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,220
Maybe I imagined it.

269
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:25,680
Shutter...

270
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:28,620
I had no idea you were so troubled.

271
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:30,840
Stay at my place tonight.

272
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:31,580
Yeah.

273
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:33,400
Don't worry.

274
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:37,520
My wife will cook for you,
and the bath's huge too.

275
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:38,200
Yeah.

276
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:46,880
Granny, this is Shutter-kun. We're looking after him for a while,
for reasons.

277
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:47,960
Nice to meet you.

278
00:16:48,820 --> 00:16:49,540
Nice to meet you, please take care of me.

279
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:51,600
Well, what a good boy.

280
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:54,300
You're not Ryo-san's secret child, are you?

281
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,980
Don't say such stupid things.

282
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:59,760
Right, you don't even have a
woman who could become his mother.

283
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:00,080
Oh my.

284
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:02,920
What's that? Someone suspicious.

285
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:07,000
See? A huge bath, right?

286
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,680
It's the first time I've
relaxed in a big bath like this.

287
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:12,420
Even when we go to a hot spring,

288
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:15,080
they make us hold placards
at the corners and such.

289
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:16,360
I see, I guess.

290
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:18,840
As long as Dad has his videos,

291
00:17:18,840 --> 00:17:21,100
he wouldn't even care if I disappeared.

292
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:23,380
That's not true.
He's surely worrying about you right now.

293
00:17:25,300 --> 00:17:25,860
Who's there?

294
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:34,060
You!

295
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:39,440
Sigh...

296
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:42,500
That's definitely a serious injury.

297
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:45,940
This guy might need some drastic treatment

298
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:57,500
It flew away!

299
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:58,820
Shall we go somewhere?

300
00:17:58,820 --> 00:18:00,360
See you, bye-bye.

301
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:05,040
S-Shutter...

302
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:06,920
He looked so full of life...

303
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:20,660
This is a kidnapping.

304
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:24,060
Shutter-kun has been kidnapped.

305
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:25,820
So what did the culprit say?

306
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:30,000
Well, I was filming Shutter when...

307
00:18:30,740 --> 00:18:34,200
They demanded all 5,500 videotapes.

308
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:37,140
But why would they want videotapes?

309
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:40,840
There must be something
on the footage you shot.

310
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:41,780
I see.

311
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:44,940
You must have accidentally filmed
the scene of a crime or something.

312
00:18:44,940 --> 00:18:46,200
N-no way.

313
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:49,900
These tapes hold my and Shutter's memories.

314
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:50,480
Dear.

315
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:53,260
Anyway, we don't have time to dawdle.

316
00:18:57,820 --> 00:18:58,540
Got it.

317
00:18:58,540 --> 00:18:59,540
Let's go.

318
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:00,580
Yeah.

319
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:15,320
Darling,

320
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:28,340
did you bring what we agreed on?

321
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:30,300
It's all in here.

322
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:31,400
Let me see.

323
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:34,360
Good.

324
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:35,940
Where's Shutter?

325
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:37,420
Where is Shutter?

326
00:19:49,540 --> 00:19:52,720
What time did I film you?

327
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,180
Hand over those videotapes right now.

328
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:56,960
I said all of them, so it's all of them!

329
00:19:57,820 --> 00:19:58,540
A-all of them?

330
00:19:58,940 --> 00:20:01,680
But these contain everything about Shutter.

331
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:03,080
They're our treasure.

332
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:04,500
They're our treasure.

333
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:04,880
They're our treasure.

334
00:20:06,100 --> 00:20:06,460
They're our treasure.

335
00:20:06,460 --> 00:20:06,500
They're our treasure.

336
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:06,760
They're our treasure.

337
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:07,000
They're our treasure.

338
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:07,680
They're our treasure.

339
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:08,160
They're our treasure.

340
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:09,900
They're our treasure.

341
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:10,480
W-what about it?

342
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:12,980
What's wrong? Spit it out!

343
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:14,040
Y-yeah.

344
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:19,780
Senpai, aren't Volvo-san
and Sakonji-san going too far?

345
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:22,720
Yeah, Ryo-chan. That's a bit harsh.

346
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:26,080
No, he won't understand
unless we go this far.

347
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:30,340
Tell me, your videos or your son?
Which is it?

348
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:32,720
I-it's...

349
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:34,120
Dad!

350
00:20:39,920 --> 00:21:06,820
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!
Eh eh eh eh eh eh eh

351
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:07,560
Here we come!

352
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:09,400
There he is!

353
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:11,560
We're coming!

354
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,240
Eek!

355
00:21:18,420 --> 00:21:19,100
Shutter-kun!

356
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:20,260
Ryo-san!

357
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:21,800
Hit the brakes already!

358
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:25,020
It's no good, the toy gun got caught in it!

359
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:26,940
Damn, it's a wreck.

360
00:21:26,940 --> 00:21:27,666
Shutter-kun,

361
00:21:27,716 --> 00:21:31,080
I'm jumping over to your side,
so hold the steering wheel tight!

362
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:32,840
O-okay, got it.

363
00:21:33,300 --> 00:21:33,880
Here goes!

364
00:21:37,820 --> 00:21:38,360
Ryo-san!

365
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:39,880
The sea!

366
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:41,960
What?!

367
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:47,440
Dad...

368
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:49,360
Shutter...

369
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:55,280
Shutter!

370
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,800
Dad! Dad!

371
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:01,500
It's okay now, it's all right!

372
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:13,560
Your dad's tapes

373
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:14,720
It's fine now.

374
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:18,060
Besides, the shutter's gotten heavy

375
00:22:18,060 --> 00:22:23,120
Now that I think about it, I haven't held
you like this for quite a while, have I?

376
00:22:23,500 --> 00:22:24,220
Dear.

377
00:22:24,220 --> 00:22:26,020
Asako.

378
00:22:26,020 --> 00:22:28,960
Dear, about all this...

379
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:32,220
I know. It was all an act, wasn't it?

380
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:33,520
I'm sorry.

381
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:36,280
No, I'm the one who should apologize.

382
00:22:37,820 --> 00:22:41,240
Until now,
I've been so consumed with shooting videos

383
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:44,200
that I never gave a
thought to how you two felt.

384
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,080
I've come to my senses.

385
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:47,040
Dear.

386
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:48,400
Dear.

387
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:54,840
That was close at the end, though.

388
00:22:55,320 --> 00:22:56,780
And that wraps everything up

389
00:22:57,600 --> 00:23:00,200
All our hard work paid off after all.

390
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:03,980
Honestly, playing villains
like this suits us perfectly.

391
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:04,900
Oh my.

392
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:08,160
You two looked even more
the part than the real thing.

393
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:14,740
Hey, didn't somebody forget about someone?

394
00:23:17,260 --> 00:23:20,640
I never realized Shutter
had become so heavy.

395
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:27,280
I've truly come to realize what a foolish parent I was,
only ever seeing my child through a camera viewfinder.

396
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:30,900
You can't feel a child's weight through a video,
can you.

397
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:34,000
By the way,
are you three going out somewhere today?

398
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:35,920
Yes, to the amusement park.

399
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:38,120
Without bringing any cameras, empty-handed.

400
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:41,780
We'll keep the memories in our hearts,
just between us.

401
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:47,560
Sounds like it'll make some good memories.

402
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:50,200
After all, rather than just hearing
old stories or watching videos,

403
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:53,380
it's better to have your parents tell you about them in person,
isn't it.

404
00:24:13,560 --> 00:24:20,060
Even in the dead of night, calls come in

405
00:24:20,060 --> 00:24:27,340
If it's you, I wake up feeling good

406
00:24:28,020 --> 00:24:31,760
Even dull conversations

407
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:36,560
set my whole body on fire

408
00:24:36,780 --> 00:24:42,840
But I want to see my friends

409
00:24:43,360 --> 00:24:47,260
I surely want to be loved

410
00:24:47,640 --> 00:24:52,600
To the point that everyone
gets a little annoyed

411
00:24:52,600 --> 00:24:58,300
Feeling like we're melting into one another

412
00:24:58,860 --> 00:25:02,140
I surely want to confide

413
00:25:02,740 --> 00:25:07,900
Somehow, only love is out of tune

414
00:25:08,500 --> 00:25:11,540
Even my bravado

415
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:15,760
Don't hide it all

416
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:24,800
You know, I've made it a rule: on night shifts,
it's cup noodles.

417
00:25:24,800 --> 00:25:26,760
Cup noodles are the ultimate midnight snack.

418
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:34,080
It's a miraculous taste, so please,
just let me eat my cup noodles in peace.

419
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:37,760
Next time,
be gentle with Kameari's nights, will you?

